    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch09-item-1-3-1",
      "sourceStart": 2580,
      "sourceEnd": 2729,
      "original": "#### 1.3.1. <span style=\"color: red\">(Determinant)</span> Let $n=\\dim V\\geq1$. For $\\alpha\\in V_{\\mathrm{alt}}^{(n)}$ and $T\\in\\mathcal L(V)$, define",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch09-block-0011",
      "sourceStart": 2729,
      "sourceEnd": 3236,
      "sha256": "362e0fbc60e60adc0dc3d8a6d0e84911966290a2a33b899ddc3e6189142c3924"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch09-item-1-3-2",
      "sourceStart": 3236,
      "sourceEnd": 3414,
      "original": "#### 1.3.2. <span style=\"color: red\">(Characteristic polynomial)</span> Suppose $T \\in \\mathcal{L}(V)$. The polynomial defined as follows is called the characteristic polynomial.",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
