    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch09-item-1-4-1",
      "sourceStart": 3470,
      "sourceEnd": 3606,
      "original": "#### 1.4.1. Let $\\mathcal{B}(V_1,\\ldots,V_m)$ denote the set of all $m$-linear forms $\\beta:V_1 \\times \\cdots \\times V_m \\rightarrow F$.",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch09-block-0014",
      "sourceStart": 3606,
      "sourceEnd": 3608,
      "sha256": "75a11da44c802486bc6f65640aa48a730f0f684c5c07a42ba3cd1735eb3fb070"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch09-item-1-4-2",
      "sourceStart": 3608,
      "sourceEnd": 3845,
      "original": "#### 1.4.2. <span style=\"color: red\">(Tensor product)</span> Let $V_1 \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes V_m:=\\mathcal{B}(V_1',\\ldots,V_m')$. The tensor product $v_1 \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes v_m \\in \\mathcal{B}(V_1',\\ldots,V_m')$ is defined as follows",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch09-block-0015",
      "sourceStart": 3845,
      "sourceEnd": 4017,
      "sha256": "5705c11450a896e424aa9e69838793d1bef9a0ac00d248486add450cb2bba349"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch09-item-1-4-3",
      "sourceStart": 4017,
      "sourceEnd": 4252,
      "original": "#### 1.4.3. <span style=\"color: red\">(Inner product of tensor product)</span> Suppose $V_1,\\ldots,V_m$ are inner product spaces. Then define the inner product on $V_1 \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes V_m$ as the one that satisfies the following:",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch09-block-0016",
      "sourceStart": 4252,
      "sourceEnd": 4661,
      "sha256": "9daacf9550c091484d11ac0a6280aadf551bf33bc07b780636d9d2ede3529027"
    },
    {
