    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch09-block-0018",
      "sourceStart": 4720,
      "sourceEnd": 4722,
      "sha256": "75a11da44c802486bc6f65640aa48a730f0f684c5c07a42ba3cd1735eb3fb070"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch09-item-2-1-1",
      "sourceStart": 4722,
      "sourceEnd": 4855,
      "original": "#### 2.1.1. Suppose $\\beta$ is a bilinear form on $V$ and $T\\in\\mathcal{L}(V)$. Define bilinear forms $\\alpha$ and $\\gamma$ on $V$ by",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch09-block-0019",
      "sourceStart": 4855,
      "sourceEnd": 5128,
      "sha256": "633c7e8b5c1363161e593aa782cc34900f6999ecb73af7f5f845d9962a11e2a7"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch09-item-2-1-2",
      "sourceStart": 5128,
      "sourceEnd": 5322,
      "original": "#### 2.1.2. <span style=\"color: red\">(Change of basis formula)</span> Suppose $\\beta \\in V^{(2)}$. Suppose $\\mathscr{B}=\\{e_1,\\ldots,e_n\\},\\ \\mathscr{C}=\\{f_1,\\ldots,f_n\\}$ are bases of $V$. Let",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch09-block-0020",
      "sourceStart": 5322,
      "sourceEnd": 5704,
      "sha256": "b14b266bf424a6a2fbe9151f9c1762605bdd6e118880c9f112fce486d71b03e3"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch09-item-2-1-3",
      "sourceStart": 5704,
      "sourceEnd": 5789,
      "original": "#### 2.1.3. Suppose $\\rho \\in V^{(2)}$. Then the following statements are equivalent.",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch09-block-0021",
      "sourceStart": 5789,
      "sourceEnd": 6100,
      "sha256": "40532f2376654da2f5a2d02ac29cfd6c38cea3263d0cdba3630831944a839793"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch09-item-2-1-4",
      "sourceStart": 6100,
      "sourceEnd": 6304,
      "original": "#### 2.1.4. Suppose $F=\\mathbb{R}$ and $V$ is an inner product space. Let $\\rho \\in V_{\\mathrm{sym}}^{(2)}$. Then there exists an orthonormal basis $\\mathscr{B}$ where $M_{\\mathscr{B}}(\\rho)$ is diagonal.",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch09-block-0022",
      "sourceStart": 6304,
      "sourceEnd": 6306,
      "sha256": "75a11da44c802486bc6f65640aa48a730f0f684c5c07a42ba3cd1735eb3fb070"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch09-item-2-1-5",
      "sourceStart": 6306,
      "sourceEnd": 6380,
      "original": "#### 2.1.5. $V^{(2)}=V_{\\mathrm{sym}}^{(2)}\\oplus V_{\\mathrm{alt}}^{(2)}$.",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch09-block-0023",
      "sourceStart": 6380,
      "sourceEnd": 6382,
      "sha256": "75a11da44c802486bc6f65640aa48a730f0f684c5c07a42ba3cd1735eb3fb070"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch09-item-2-1-6",
      "sourceStart": 6382,
      "sourceEnd": 6502,
      "original": "#### 2.1.6. Suppose $V=F^n$. $q$ is a quadratic form on $V$ if and only if there exists $A \\in F^{n \\times n}$ such that",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch09-block-0024",
      "sourceStart": 6502,
      "sourceEnd": 6569,
      "sha256": "2516c330cc69fb68c93f603f3f57b147e98390bb25d2989f970ced3d3285928c"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch09-item-2-1-7",
      "sourceStart": 6569,
      "sourceEnd": 6724,
      "original": "#### 2.1.7. Suppose $q:V\\to F$. Then $q$ is a quadratic form if and only if there exists a unique $\\rho \\in V_{\\mathrm{sym}}^{(2)}$ such that $q = q_\\rho$.",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch09-block-0025",
      "sourceStart": 6724,
      "sourceEnd": 6726,
      "sha256": "75a11da44c802486bc6f65640aa48a730f0f684c5c07a42ba3cd1735eb3fb070"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch09-item-2-1-8",
      "sourceStart": 6726,
      "sourceEnd": 6775,
      "original": "#### 2.1.8. Suppose $q$ is a quadratic form. Then",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch09-block-0026",
      "sourceStart": 6775,
      "sourceEnd": 7078,
      "sha256": "d71d16ac5182062d94d6f8a30838b6a7ee2173cf38942c57317046e14c745041"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch09-section-2-2",
      "sourceStart": 7078,
      "sourceEnd": 7116,
      "original": "### 2.2. Alternating Multilinear Forms",
      "action": "moved-to-section-title"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch09-block-0027",
      "sourceStart": 7116,
      "sourceEnd": 7118,
      "sha256": "75a11da44c802486bc6f65640aa48a730f0f684c5c07a42ba3cd1735eb3fb070"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch09-item-2-2-1",
      "sourceStart": 7118,
      "sourceEnd": 7223,
      "original": "#### 2.2.1. Suppose $\\alpha \\in V_{\\mathrm{alt}}^{(m)}$ and $v_1,\\ldots,v_m$ are linearly dependent. Then",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch09-block-0028",
      "sourceStart": 7223,
      "sourceEnd": 7327,
      "sha256": "8e40ab7cdbd711dc9538fb6d2d863aff6551959ad037e53395bbf87aa80c54ea"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch09-item-2-2-2",
      "sourceStart": 7327,
      "sourceEnd": 7436,
      "original": "#### 2.2.2. Suppose $\\alpha \\in V_{\\mathrm{alt}}^{(m)}$. For every $\\sigma\\in S_m$ and $v_1,\\ldots,v_m\\in V$,",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch09-block-0029",
      "sourceStart": 7436,
      "sourceEnd": 7636,
      "sha256": "217dfe8351c2ce628f750641e641db253e552a4469c01adde4e4874de756c4e2"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch09-item-2-2-3",
      "sourceStart": 7636,
      "sourceEnd": 7784,
      "original": "#### 2.2.3. Let $n=\\dim(V)$. Let $e_1,\\ldots,e_n$ be a basis of $V$, $\\varphi_1,\\ldots,\\varphi_n$ be the dual basis and $v_1,\\ldots,v_n \\in V$. Then",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch09-block-0030",
      "sourceStart": 7784,
      "sourceEnd": 8035,
      "sha256": "a60a9b01493a45117d600bcac9863fed136b48342f986d9f50234ddc12be298f"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch09-item-2-2-4",
      "sourceStart": 8035,
      "sourceEnd": 8255,
      "original": "#### 2.2.4. Suppose $n=\\dim(V),\\alpha \\in V_{\\mathrm{alt}}^{(n)}$ is nonzero and $e_1,\\ldots,e_n$ is a list of vectors in $V$. Then $\\alpha(e_1,\\ldots,e_n) \\neq 0$ if and only if $e_1,\\ldots,e_n$ is linearly independent.",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch09-block-0031",
      "sourceStart": 8255,
      "sourceEnd": 8257,
      "sha256": "75a11da44c802486bc6f65640aa48a730f0f684c5c07a42ba3cd1735eb3fb070"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch09-section-2-3",
      "sourceStart": 8257,
      "sourceEnd": 8278,
      "original": "### 2.3. Determinants",
      "action": "moved-to-section-title"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch09-block-0032",
      "sourceStart": 8278,
      "sourceEnd": 8280,
      "sha256": "75a11da44c802486bc6f65640aa48a730f0f684c5c07a42ba3cd1735eb3fb070"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch09-item-2-3-1",
      "sourceStart": 8280,
      "sourceEnd": 8391,
      "original": "#### 2.3.1. The map $(v_1,\\ldots,v_n) \\mapsto \\det(v_1,\\ldots,v_n)$ is an alternating $n$-linear form on $F^n$.",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch09-block-0033",
      "sourceStart": 8391,
      "sourceEnd": 8393,
      "sha256": "75a11da44c802486bc6f65640aa48a730f0f684c5c07a42ba3cd1735eb3fb070"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch09-item-2-3-2",
      "sourceStart": 8393,
      "sourceEnd": 8437,
      "original": "#### 2.3.2. Let $A \\in F^{n \\times n}$. Then",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch09-block-0034",
      "sourceStart": 8437,
      "sourceEnd": 8673,
      "sha256": "db4fe3527b692ae9c2024392eb2d93ec43ee708496488a659ff3e961bcaf9f19"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch09-item-2-3-3",
      "sourceStart": 8673,
      "sourceEnd": 8808,
      "original": "#### 2.3.3. <span style=\"color: red\">(Properties of determinants)</span> Suppose $S,T \\in \\mathcal{L}(V)$ and $A,B \\in F^{n \\times n}$.",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch09-block-0035",
      "sourceStart": 8808,
      "sourceEnd": 9588,
      "sha256": "6a8880b7248f4d6fd9be1229eef62dedf8dbcf647aee018fb822183e3ca22ee1"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
