    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch09-item-2-3-6",
      "sourceStart": 10018,
      "sourceEnd": 10170,
      "original": "#### 2.3.6. <span style=\"color: red\">(Cayley-Hamilton theorem)</span> Let $q$ be the characteristic polynomial of $T \\in \\mathcal{L}(V)$. Then $q(T)=0$.",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
