      "sourceStart": 11103,
      "sourceEnd": 11340,
      "sha256": "63afbbaf8e495cb7a733e43e03c97b2120bd3ba455551ca3e685134b717d5123"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch09-item-2-4-3",
      "sourceStart": 11340,
      "sourceEnd": 11543,
      "original": "#### 2.4.3. Suppose $\\Gamma : V_1 \\times \\cdots \\times V_m \\rightarrow U$ is an $m$-linear map. Then there exists a unique linear map $\\hat{\\Gamma}:V_1 \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes V_m \\rightarrow U$ such that",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "blockId": "la-ch09-block-0045",
      "sourceStart": 11543,
      "sourceEnd": 11864,
      "sha256": "44ae85c381954e068175edb8dbd81b575c62e87c9bef664ddb4ce4694f5eec8b"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "id": "la-ch09-item-2-4-4",
      "sourceStart": 11864,
      "sourceEnd": 12023,
      "original": "#### 2.4.4. Suppose $V$ and $W$ are inner product spaces, and let $e_1,\\ldots,e_m$ and $f_1,\\ldots,f_n$ be orthonormal bases of $V$ and $W$, respectively. Then",
      "action": "moved-to-item-title-and-statement"
